From 5db1f005f0951a8a1961775bc28a31e1594f0f7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:40:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Wallguard/Dreadwatch sources: the API key inside the address
 ($APIkey)

Owner 2026-10-28: the second form of API source. Some suppliers take the key
in the list's URL rather than in a request header, e.g.
https://api.qfeeds.com/api?feed_type=malware_domains&api_token=$APIkey or
https://threatfox-api.abuse.ch/v2/files/exports/$APIkey/hostfile.txt. A key
field alone cannot say where in the URL it belongs, so the URL says it: the
user types $APIkey at the point of insertion and saves the key as before.

- wallguard.sh fetch (shared by both tools): a URL with $APIkey needs the
  slot's saved key (99 without one, as a header source). Each $APIkey becomes
  the key, %-encoded outside [A-Za-z0-9._~-]; the finished URL is written into
  the same root-only 0600 curl config as url = "...", removed after the fetch,
  and curl is called with no URL argument - the key is never in a command
  line (awk reads it from its environment, readable by root only). A header
  and $APIkey together both carry the key.
- The one "$" a source URL may carry is $APIkey, and never in the host:
  httpd sh_url(), rc sh_url_ok() (Wallguard) and Dreadwatch's update.sh
  line check agree; any other "$" is refused as before.
- Pages (Wallguard, Dreadwatch): one hint line under the form (RSHD_163, 25
  packs, after RSHD_162); a URL with $APIkey is valid, needs a key (or keeps
  the saved one) and is not cleared for lacking a header; its row shows API /
  key saved.
- Keys stay write-only in /jffs/wallguard/keys and /jffs/rwarden/dnskeys,
  unchanged (src_keys_save keeps a key per live slot).

Tests (lean): test_wallguard_sources.py (fetch under sh + busybox ash:
encoding, query and path forms, both placeholders, no key -> 99, header +
URL, 0600 + cleanup; httpd and rc validators share one URL table; page and
packs) and test_dreadwatch_sources.py (update.sh end to end with a $APIkey
source and a host-placeholder line that is skipped).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
